{"comparisons":[],"failures":[],"frontier":[],"initial":{"alternatives":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines private market assets and identifies direct and indirect exposure routes relevant to aggregation.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u1.5"},{"reason":"Establishes the Fund and manager scope and distinguishes disclosure requirements from possible scrutiny and classification.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u4.564"},{"reason":"Explains the risk rationale for scrutiny; the described risks are not independent automatic classification triggers.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u7.1028"},{"reason":"States disclosure and distributor-selection expectations surrounding the selected classification control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u10.1937"},{"reason":"Heading identifies the separate enhanced-disclosure section.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u11.2466"},{"reason":"Potential exposure triggers offering-document disclosure; that trigger is broader than mandatory complex-product classification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u14.2516"},{"reason":"Exposure-disclosure examples help identify relevant evidence but supply no binding aggregation methodology.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u15.2718"},{"reason":"Underlying-asset disclosures can inform assessment of indirect exposures without determining classification themselves.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u16.2995"},{"reason":"Specific risk disclosures are a separate obligation and contextual evidence for the Fund's risk characteristics.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u17.3223"},{"reason":"Heading identifies the classification section.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u18.3743"},{"reason":"Supplies the inclusive mandatory 50% threshold and the additional case-by-case designation route.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779"},{"reason":"Aggregate exposure also informs discretionary designation below the automatic threshold.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u22.4078"},{"reason":"Strategy, composition, liquidity and risk are discretionary assessment factors, not standalone automatic triggers.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u24.4176"},{"reason":"Instrument characteristics inform designation; the examples do not classify every CLO or SRT holding automatically.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u26.4290"},{"reason":"Home-regulator conditions are relevant discretionary factors; no automatic substitution for an SFC designation is stated.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u28.4505"},{"reason":"Requires holistic assessment for the designation cases qualified by footnote 7.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u29.4630"},{"reason":"Connects classification to prevailing complex-product sales requirements, including suitability without solicitation or recommendation.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u32.4805"},{"reason":"Heading introduces target-market and distributor-selection obligations.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u33.5086"},{"reason":"Incorporates separate product-approval guidance; its full obligations are outside the selected classification predicate.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u36.5149"},{"reason":"Managers must select distributors capable of understanding classification and assigning an appropriate risk rating; risk rating is not equated with complex-product designation.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u39.5617"},{"reason":"Advertising requirements remain separate from the selected classification trigger.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u42.6275"},{"reason":"Section heading has no independent classification condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u43.6653"},{"reason":"Possible enhanced scrutiny and exclusion from FASTrack for new applications do not themselves establish complex-product status.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u46.6668"},{"reason":"Existing Funds require review, appropriate action and distributor communication; consultation is encouraged when classification is uncertain, without a specified calendar deadline.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u49.6955"},{"reason":"Identifies a clarification channel rather than a classification condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u52.7565"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing division without adding a substantive rule.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u55.7698"},{"reason":"Identifies the named institution in the retained source; no independent authenticity determination is made.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u56.7736"},{"reason":"The separate 15% direct-investment limit neither replaces the aggregate 50% classification threshold nor excludes direct investments from it.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u58.7778"},{"reason":"Prevents treating listed indirect-exposure examples as exhaustive and identifies possible future updates.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u59.7979"},{"reason":"Provides the retained BDC description but does not specify the amount of a holding counted as private-market exposure.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u60.8163"},{"reason":"Describes CLO collateral, informing exposure identification without resolving tranche-level measurement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u61.8338"},{"reason":"Identifies TRS and SRT examples; derivative exposure measurement remains unspecified.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u62.8487"},{"reason":"Excludes LAFs from this circular's Fund scope and refers their treatment to a separate unprovided circular.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691"},{"reason":"Attaches the below-50% qualification to holistic designation assessment.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"},{"reason":"Identifies sources governing downstream sales requirements; their unprovided contents cannot be reconstructed from this citation.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u65.9044"},{"reason":"Dates the referenced product-approval guidance; those dates do not establish commencement of the retained circular.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u66.9304"},{"reason":"Identifies and dates the referenced advertising guidelines as described by the source; their contents and current version are not independently established.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u67.9509"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The defined Funds are authorised for public offering in Hong Kong, with LAFs excluded. Guidance is addressed to management companies and fund managers; designation is an SFC decision and attaches to the Fund. Distribution consequences include suitability requirements, while managers must select suitably knowledgeable distributors. Scrutiny of new authorisation applications is a separate process and does not itself establish complex-product classification.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u32.4805","d4148dd852cee.u39.5617","d4148dd852cee.u46.6668"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Private market assets collectively cover private credit and private equity. Direct and indirect routes and instrument examples are supplied, and the indirect list is expressly non-exhaustive. The inclusive threshold is clear, but the retained text does not settle how fund-level holdings translate into measured underlying exposure, derivative exposure or netting. These are unresolved measurement questions, not authority to select a convenient convention. The separate 15% direct-investment limit is not the complex-product threshold and does not remove direct exposure from aggregation.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u1.5","d4148dd852cee.u15.2718","d4148dd852cee.u16.2995","d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u58.7778","d4148dd852cee.u59.7979","d4148dd852cee.u60.8163","d4148dd852cee.u61.8338","d4148dd852cee.u62.8487"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Footnote 6 excludes LAFs from the defined Fund population; it does not establish that LAFs are non-complex under their separate regime. Footnote 7 locates holistic designation assessment below 50%, rather than creating a waiver above the mandatory threshold. Exposure below 50% is therefore not a blanket exemption. The sales consequence expressly applies irrespective of solicitation or recommendation.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910","d4148dd852cee.u32.4805"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The threshold entails classification; the SFC may additionally designate individual Funds below it through holistic assessment. Aggregate exposure, strategy, portfolio, liquidity, risk, instrument characteristics and home-regulator conditions inform that discretion without becoming independent automatic classification triggers. Enhanced disclosure is separately required. Review expectations and encouraged consultation do not turn classification into an optional manager decision or make missing evidence an exemption.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u22.4078","d4148dd852cee.u24.4176","d4148dd852cee.u26.4290","d4148dd852cee.u28.4505","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u32.4805","d4148dd852cee.u49.6955"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The packet distinguishes new applications from existing Funds and expects appropriate action, including offering-document updates as soon as practicable. It supplies no calendar commencement date, fixed transition deadline, exposure observation convention or reclassification rule. The dates 30 April 2014, 4 March 2016 and April 2013 describe referenced materials, not this circular's commencement. The instruction to apply prevailing sales requirements and the possibility of updating exposure examples introduce temporal dependencies that the retained text alone cannot resolve.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u32.4805","d4148dd852cee.u46.6668","d4148dd852cee.u49.6955","d4148dd852cee.u59.7979","d4148dd852cee.u66.9304","d4148dd852cee.u67.9509"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"Referenced but unprovided materials include UT Code section 7.3, the LAF circular, Code of Conduct paragraph 5.5, Online Distribution and Advisory Platforms Guidelines chapter 6, relevant FAQs, product-approval guidance and advertising guidelines. They prevent a complete account of downstream distribution obligations and the excluded LAF regime. The packet also lists three unresolved dependency identifiers without contents or a mapping to particular references; their substance cannot be inferred. Classification additionally depends on fund-specific holdings, measurement evidence and applicable SFC decisions. The reference to paragraphs 9 and 10 cannot be mapped conclusively from the supplied unit locators alone.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u58.7778","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u65.9044","d4148dd852cee.u66.9304","d4148dd852cee.u67.9509","d4148dd852cee.u49.6955"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["What retained guidance or authoritative fund-specific assessment resolves measurement of indirect and derivative exposure for the inclusive 50% threshold?","What commencement, transition, observation-date and reclassification provisions apply, if any?","For the particular Fund, is there sufficient evidence of scope, LAF exclusion status, aggregate exposure and an applicable SFC designation to determine the selected predicate?","What are the contents and source-reference mappings of missing.7b393f53d503773a762cf757, missing.de6722b4a9f08d782e48c11a and missing.13ee048eabca24d91ac9305c?","Which versions of the referenced sales requirements and FAQs govern distribution at the relevant time, and what separate rules govern an excluded LAF?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["The formalization evaluates one particular fund at one identified assessment time; it does not determine whole-firm compliance or satisfaction of the downstream sales requirements.","Footnote 6 qualifies the defined population of Funds, and footnote 7 qualifies the holistic designation assessment in cases below 50%.","The designation fact records an actual, applicable SFC designation. A manager's view that designation is likely or appropriate does not establish that fact.","The threshold fact must be established using a supportable exposure measurement. The formalization supplies no missing valuation, look-through, aggregation or monitoring convention.","A result is interpreted only within the Boolean scope. Unknown facts are not assigned false values; one established true classification route can nevertheless establish the result without resolving the other route."],"citations":[{"quote":"This circular provides guidance to management companies of funds that are authorised by the SFC for offering to the public in Hong Kong (Funds)6 in this regard.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u4.564"},{"quote":"Except for listed closed-ended alternative asset funds (LAFs).","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691"},{"quote":"A Fund will be considered as a complex product if its total direct and indirect exposures to private market assets amount to 50% or more of the Fund’s NAV.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779"},{"quote":"On a case-by-case basis, the SFC may also designate a Fund as a complex product, taking into account factors including, without limitation:","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779"},{"quote":"In assessing whether the complex product designation is warranted7, the SFC will adopt a holistic approach taking into account the specific circumstances of the case.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u29.4630"},{"quote":"In cases where the Fund’s aggregate direct and indirect exposures to private market assets are less than 50% of the Fund’s NAV.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"},{"quote":"A Fund classified as a complex product will be subject to the SFC’s prevailing requirements for the sale of complex products8 including but not limited to ensuring the suitability of the Fund for its investors irrespective of whether solicitation or recommendation is involved.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u32.4805"},{"quote":"Fund managers are encouraged to consult the SFC at the earliest opportunity if they are in doubt regarding complex product classification of their Funds.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u49.6955"}],"distinction":"The threshold sentence uses mandatory language, while the below-threshold route requires an SFC designation and permits a holistic assessment. For example, an in-scope Fund with established aggregate exposure of exactly 50% satisfies the trigger without a separate designation. A Fund at 49% with established absence of an SFC designation does not satisfy this selected trigger merely because its CLO holdings or liquidity profile warrant scrutiny; a Fund at 49% that has actually been designated does satisfy it. An otherwise comparable LAF falls outside this circular's defined Fund scope. A Fund whose exposure or designation history is missing cannot be treated as the established 49%-and-undesignated case. Footnote 7 supports attaching holistic assessment to cases below 50%, rather than making the express 50% threshold discretionary. The strongest uncertainty is how to establish aggregate exposure for layered instruments and the relevant assessment date.","family":"modality","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"Whether the particular fund is authorised by the SFC for offering to the public in Hong Kong at the assessment time.","name":"sfc_authorised_public_fund","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u4.564"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean fund-scope fact"},{"meaning":"Whether the particular fund falls within the listed closed-ended alternative asset fund category excluded by footnote 6. An unresolved category classification remains unknown.","name":"listed_closed_ended_alternative_asset_fund","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u63.8691"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean exclusion fact"},{"meaning":"Whether established total direct and indirect exposure to private market assets amounts to at least 50% of the Fund's NAV at the assessment time. Supplying this fact requires resolving applicable exposure measurement and aggregation; missing holdings or measurement evidence is not false.","name":"aggregate_private_market_exposure_at_least_half_nav","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u1.5","d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u59.7979","d4148dd852cee.u60.8163","d4148dd852cee.u61.8338","d4148dd852cee.u62.8487"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean inclusive 50%-of-NAV threshold fact"},{"meaning":"Whether an actual SFC case-by-case designation of the particular Fund as a complex product applies at the assessment time. Mere risk factors, possible designation or an unsearched designation history do not establish a positive or negative value.","name":"applicable_sfc_complex_product_designation","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean applicable-designation fact"}],"result":"(or aggregate_private_market_exposure_at_least_half_nav applicable_sfc_complex_product_designation)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and sfc_authorised_public_fund (not listed_closed_ended_alternative_asset_fund))"},"local_id":"classification_trigger","questions":["How should indirect exposure through BDCs, CLOs, TRSs and SRTs be measured and aggregated, including look-through, derivative exposure and possible double counting?","What valuation date, monitoring frequency and treatment of temporary threshold crossings govern the 50% test?","What evidence establishes an applicable SFC designation, its effective date and any subsequent withdrawal or replacement?","Does omitted commencement or transitional material specify when existing Funds must complete classification changes and distributor communications?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] For an SFC-authorised fund offered to the public in Hong Kong that is not a listed closed-ended alternative asset fund, the classification trigger is satisfied when its aggregate direct and indirect exposure to private market assets is at least 50% of NAV, or when the SFC has actually designated it as a complex product on a case-by-case basis. True means that this circular supplies a basis requiring complex-product treatment for distribution. False, within scope and with the relevant facts established, means that neither classification route is established under this selected control; it does not establish non-complex status under every other applicable rule. Missing exposure or designation evidence remains unknown. The retained text supports one classification structure; the principal unresolved issues concern exposure measurement, timing and evidence, rather than a competing rule making every private-market exposure automatically complex.","subject":"Selected control: whether the retained circular triggers complex-product treatment for distribution of a particular Fund"}]},"controlled-language":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines private market assets and direct and indirect exposure routes.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u1.5"},{"reason":"Defines Funds and identifies management companies as the guidance's addressees.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u4.564"},{"reason":"Explains risk concerns; does not independently impose classification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u7.1028"},{"reason":"Investor information and distributor selection duties are distinct from classification triggers.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u10.1937"},{"reason":"Heading for disclosure provisions.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u11.2466"},{"reason":"Possible exposure triggers disclosure guidance, not expressly automatic complex-product classification.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u14.2516"},{"reason":"Disclosure examples use permitted exposure ranges; whether those ranges determine classification is unresolved.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u15.2718"},{"reason":"Underlying-asset disclosure requirement; not a separate classification rule.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u16.2995"},{"reason":"Risk disclosure requirement; the KFS qualification attaches to disclosure, not classification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u17.3223"},{"reason":"Identifies the classification section.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u18.3743"},{"reason":"Establishes the inclusive 50% automatic threshold and a separate SFC designation power.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779"},{"reason":"Aggregate exposure is a discretionary assessment factor.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u22.4078"},{"reason":"Strategy, composition, liquidity and risk are discretionary assessment factors.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u24.4176"},{"reason":"Asset characteristics are discretionary assessment factors.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u26.4290"},{"reason":"Home-regulator distribution conditions inform discretion; they are not stated exceptions.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u28.4505"},{"reason":"Requires a holistic case-specific assessment for designation.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u29.4630"},{"reason":"Classification activates prevailing complex-product sale requirements, including suitability without solicitation or recommendation.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u32.4805"},{"reason":"Heading for separate target-market and distributor duties.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u33.5086"},{"reason":"References separate product-approval requirements whose full contents are absent.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u36.5149"},{"reason":"Requires distributor knowledge of classification; does not confer the SFC's designation power on distributors.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u39.5617"},{"reason":"Advertising duties are separate from the selected classification control.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u42.6275"},{"reason":"Section heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u43.6653"},{"reason":"Closer authorisation scrutiny and possible FASTrack exclusion do not themselves establish complex-product classification.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u46.6668"},{"reason":"Existing funds must be reviewed under the stated expectations; consultation is encouraged and no fixed classification deadline is supplied.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u49.6955"},{"reason":"Identifies a clarification channel without resolving classification uncertainty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u52.7565"},{"reason":"Issuing division identification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u55.7698"},{"reason":"Issuer identification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u56.7736"},{"reason":"States a separate 15% direct-investment limit; this does not replace the aggregate 50% classification threshold.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u58.7778"},{"reason":"Indirect-exposure examples are non-exhaustive and may change.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u59.7979"},{"reason":"Defines BDCs for the exposure examples.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u60.8163"},{"reason":"Defines CLOs for the exposure examples.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u61.8338"},{"reason":"Identifies derivative exposure examples without specifying exposure measurement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u62.8487"},{"reason":"Excludes LAFs from the defined Funds; their separate circular is absent.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691"},{"reason":"Attaches the holistic designation assessment to aggregate exposure below 50%.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"},{"reason":"Identifies downstream sale-rule sources; their complete requirements cannot be reconstructed here.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u65.9044"},{"reason":"Dates concern the referenced product-approval circular, not this circular's commencement.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u66.9304"},{"reason":"Date concerns the referenced advertising guidelines, not this circular's commencement.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u67.9509"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The selected control concerns classification of funds authorised for public offering in Hong Kong, excluding LAFs. Management companies receive the guidance; the SFC exercises discretionary designation; managers and distributors have related distribution responsibilities.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u39.5617","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Private market assets comprise private credit and private equity. Direct and indirect exposures aggregate, and indirect examples are non-exhaustive. The packet does not specify valuation, look-through, derivative exposure measurement, netting, or whether permitted rather than current exposure determines the threshold.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u1.5","d4148dd852cee.u15.2718","d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u59.7979","d4148dd852cee.u60.8163","d4148dd852cee.u61.8338","d4148dd852cee.u62.8487"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The LAF exclusion attaches to the definition of Funds. Footnote 7 limits the referenced holistic designation assessment to exposure below 50%; it does not qualify the automatic threshold. No exemption based on ratings, liquidity or absence of solicitation is stated.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u32.4805","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"Exposure of at least 50% produces mandatory classification. Below 50%, the SFC may designate following a holistic assessment; listed factors do not mechanically compel designation. Encouraged consultation is not a condition precedent to automatic classification.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u22.4078","d4148dd852cee.u24.4176","d4148dd852cee.u26.4290","d4148dd852cee.u28.4505","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u49.6955","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"No issue date, commencement date, measurement frequency, temporary-breach treatment or declassification rule is supplied. 'As soon as practicable' appears in existing-fund remediation guidance, including document updates, and supplies no fixed classification grace period. Dates of referenced instruments do not resolve these gaps.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u49.6955","d4148dd852cee.u66.9304","d4148dd852cee.u67.9509"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The classification threshold is stated locally, but the separate LAF regime and full prevailing sale requirements require absent materials. The packet also lists three unresolved dependency identifiers without mapping them to particular references. Their contents cannot be assumed.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u32.4805","d4148dd852cee.u36.5149","d4148dd852cee.u58.7778","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u65.9044","d4148dd852cee.u66.9304","d4148dd852cee.u67.9509"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does the 50% test use current measured exposure, the authorised investment mandate's maximum exposure, or another specified basis? The classification sentence describes exposures that 'amount to' the threshold, whereas disclosure examples describe investment ranges.","How must indirect and derivative exposures be measured and aggregated, including look-through, leverage, netting, overlapping exposures and valuation dates?","What evidence establishes an operative SFC designation, and what rules govern its withdrawal or continued effect after exposures change?","When did the circular take effect, how frequently is classification reassessed, and how are temporary threshold crossings treated?","Which references correspond to missing.7b393f53d503773a762cf757, missing.de6722b4a9f08d782e48c11a and missing.13ee048eabca24d91ac9305c?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["This proposal answers only whether either classification route stated in the retained circular is satisfied for a fund within its defined scope.","All facts refer to the same assessment occasion. The packet does not supply the governing assessment date or measurement protocol.","The threshold fact is supplied only after the applicable exposure basis has been established; it is not inferred from the existence of private-market exposure or from disclosure examples.","An operative SFC designation requires evidence of the SFC's decision. Risk factors, consultation, closer scrutiny and missing records do not establish or negate that decision.","A false scope excludes the fund from this selected control; it does not classify the fund as non-complex under another regime."],"citations":[{"quote":"funds that are authorised by the SFC for offering to the public in Hong Kong (Funds)6","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u4.564"},{"quote":"private credit and private equity (collectively, private market assets)","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u1.5"},{"quote":"A Fund will be considered as a complex product if its total direct and indirect exposures to private market assets amount to 50% or more of the Fund’s NAV.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779"},{"quote":"On a case-by-case basis, the SFC may also designate a Fund as a complex product, taking into account factors including, without limitation:","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779"},{"quote":"In assessing whether the complex product designation is warranted7, the SFC will adopt a holistic approach taking into account the specific circumstances of the case.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u29.4630"},{"quote":"7 In cases where the Fund’s aggregate direct and indirect exposures to private market assets are less than 50% of the Fund’s NAV.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"},{"quote":"6 Except for listed closed-ended alternative asset funds (LAFs).","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691"},{"quote":"including but not limited to ensuring the suitability of the Fund for its investors irrespective of whether solicitation or recommendation is involved.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u32.4805"},{"quote":"Fund managers are encouraged to consult the SFC at the earliest opportunity if they are in doubt regarding complex product classification of their Funds.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u49.6955"}],"distinction":"The source supports two distinct routes, rather than two rival interpretations of the 50% rule: automatic classification at or above 50%, and discretionary SFC designation below it. Below-threshold exposure alone does not establish non-complex status. The strongest unresolved interpretive issue is the exposure measurement basis: current exposure and permitted exposure can yield different threshold outcomes, but the packet does not adequately specify a competing executable measurement rule.","family":"modality","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"Whether the assessed fund is authorised by the SFC for offering to the public in Hong Kong.","name":"authorised_public_hk","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u4.564"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether the assessed fund is a listed closed-ended alternative asset fund within the footnote 6 exclusion.","name":"is_laf","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u63.8691"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether the fund's total direct and indirect exposure to private credit and private equity amounts to at least 50% of its NAV on the applicable assessment basis. Unknown if the exposure evidence or governing measurement basis is unresolved.","name":"aggregate_exposure_at_least_50_percent","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u1.5","d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u59.7979","d4148dd852cee.u62.8487"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean; underlying threshold is 50 percent of NAV"},{"meaning":"Whether an SFC case-specific designation of the fund as a complex product under this circular is operative at the assessment occasion. A possible designation or absence of designation evidence leaves this fact unknown.","name":"operative_sfc_designation","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(or aggregate_exposure_at_least_50_percent operative_sfc_designation)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and authorised_public_hk (not is_laf))"},"local_id":"classification_routes","questions":["What measurement evidence supports the aggregate threshold fact for the assessed fund?","Is there evidence establishing or excluding an operative case-specific SFC designation?","Does any absent guidance specify a mandate-based test, a reassessment interval or a declassification procedure?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] For an in-scope Fund, true means the retained circular's selected complex-product classification condition is satisfied: aggregate direct and indirect private-market exposure is at least 50% of NAV, or an operative SFC case-specific designation applies. The Fund must then be treated as complex for distribution under this control. False means both routes are established to be absent at the assessment occasion; it does not establish non-complex status under all other rules. Missing exposure or designation evidence remains unknown unless a known satisfied route already determines the result. This predicate does not assess compliance with the resulting sale requirements.","subject":"Selected control: complex-product classification for distribution under the retained circular"}]},"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines private market assets and direct and indirect exposure routes.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u1.5"},{"reason":"Defines Funds and management-company scope; distinguishes disclosure duties from possible classification.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u4.564"},{"reason":"Explains classification risk considerations without establishing an independent trigger.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u7.1028"},{"reason":"Investor information and distributor selection expectations do not independently determine classification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u10.1937"},{"reason":"Disclosure section heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u11.2466"},{"reason":"Potential exposure triggers disclosure guidance, not automatic complex-product classification.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u14.2516"},{"reason":"Disclosure of exposure extent and access may support classification assessment; illustrative percentages supply no actual classification evidence.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u15.2718"},{"reason":"Underlying asset disclosures may support exposure assessment.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u16.2995"},{"reason":"Risk disclosure requirements remain distinct from the classification trigger.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u17.3223"},{"reason":"Identifies the classification section.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u18.3743"},{"reason":"Establishes the inclusive 50% mandatory threshold and additional discretionary designation route.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779"},{"reason":"Aggregate exposure is a discretionary assessment factor.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u22.4078"},{"reason":"Strategy, composition, liquidity and risk inform discretionary assessment.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u24.4176"},{"reason":"Asset characteristics inform discretionary assessment; no automatic tranche or rating trigger is supplied.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u26.4290"},{"reason":"Home-regulator conditions are factors, not stated automatic classification rules.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u28.4505"},{"reason":"Requires holistic assessment of discretionary designation.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u29.4630"},{"reason":"Classification engages prevailing complex-product sales requirements, including suitability irrespective of solicitation or recommendation.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u32.4805"},{"reason":"Target-market and distributor-selection section heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u33.5086"},{"reason":"Separate product-approval requirements are incorporated by reference; their full content is absent.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u36.5149"},{"reason":"Managers should choose distributors with knowledge of the Fund, including its complex-product status; this does not grant distributors the SFC's designation discretion.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u39.5617"},{"reason":"Advertising obligations are separate from classification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u42.6275"},{"reason":"Section heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u43.6653"},{"reason":"Closer authorisation scrutiny and possible FASTrack exclusion are distinct from complex-product classification.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u46.6668"},{"reason":"Existing funds require review and appropriate action as soon as practicable; consultation is encouraged where classification is doubtful.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u49.6955"},{"reason":"Identifies a clarification route, not a classification condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u52.7565"},{"reason":"Issuing division identification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u55.7698"},{"reason":"Issuing institution identification.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u56.7736"},{"reason":"The separate 15% direct-investment limit does not replace the 50% aggregate classification threshold; UT Code details are unavailable.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u58.7778"},{"reason":"Indirect exposure examples are expressly non-exhaustive and may be updated.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u59.7979"},{"reason":"Defines BDCs for the exposure examples.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u60.8163"},{"reason":"Defines CLOs for the exposure examples.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u61.8338"},{"reason":"Provides derivative exposure examples, including TRSs and SRTs.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u62.8487"},{"reason":"Excludes LAFs from the defined Funds and directs them to a separate circular whose rules are unavailable.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691"},{"reason":"Attaches the below-50% qualification to holistic discretionary assessment, not to the mandatory threshold.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"},{"reason":"Identifies external sales requirements; their complete content and relevant FAQs are absent.","status":"DEFERRED","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u65.9044"},{"reason":"Dates concern the referenced product-approval circular, not commencement of this circular.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u66.9304"},{"reason":"April 2013 concerns the referenced advertising guidelines, not commencement of this circular.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u67.9509"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"Classification concerns funds authorised for public offering in Hong Kong, excluding LAFs. Guidance addresses managers; SFC discretion and the resulting distribution obligations have distinct actors.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u32.4805","d4148dd852cee.u39.5617"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Private market assets comprise private credit and private equity. Direct and indirect exposures aggregate, with non-exhaustive indirect examples. The strongest unresolved issue is how instrument positions translate into measured exposure: the packet does not specify look-through, netting, leverage, double counting or valuation conventions.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u1.5","d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u59.7979","d4148dd852cee.u60.8163","d4148dd852cee.u61.8338","d4148dd852cee.u62.8487"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The LAF exclusion attaches to the defined Funds. Below 50% is not an exemption from designation: footnote 7 identifies the domain of holistic discretionary assessment. The 15% direct-investment limit is a separate constraint.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910","d4148dd852cee.u58.7778"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"At least 50% entails classification; below that threshold the SFC may designate case by case. Risk factors do not themselves establish a designation. Disclosure, distributor selection, authorisation scrutiny and encouraged consultation have separate modalities and triggers.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u22.4078","d4148dd852cee.u24.4176","d4148dd852cee.u26.4290","d4148dd852cee.u28.4505","d4148dd852cee.u46.6668","d4148dd852cee.u49.6955"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"No commencement date, measurement frequency, threshold-breach duration or declassification rule is supplied. Existing-fund actions are expected as soon as practicable. Dates attached to external documents do not establish this circular's effective date.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u49.6955","d4148dd852cee.u66.9304","d4148dd852cee.u67.9509"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The LAF circular, UT Code, sales codes and FAQs, product-approval circular and advertising guidelines are referenced but not supplied. Three missing dependency identifiers have no source hashes or mapping to particular references. Full downstream duties and external classification grounds cannot be resolved.","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u58.7778","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u65.9044","d4148dd852cee.u36.5149","d4148dd852cee.u66.9304","d4148dd852cee.u42.6275","d4148dd852cee.u67.9509"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["What exposure-calculation methodology applies to BDCs, CLOs, TRSs and SRTs, including look-through, leverage, netting and avoidance of double counting?","Does the threshold use current holdings, permitted maximum exposure or another measure, and at what valuation and assessment times?","What commencement, transition, monitoring and declassification rules apply?","For the particular Fund, what evidence establishes its scope, measured aggregate exposure and any operative SFC designation?","Which referenced documents correspond to missing.7b393f53d503773a762cf757, missing.de6722b4a9f08d782e48c11a and missing.13ee048eabca24d91ac9305c, and what relevant provisions do they contain?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["This proposal evaluates only the retained circular's classification routes for one Fund at a specified assessment time.","The circular is applicable at that assessment time; the packet does not establish commencement.","The threshold fact must be supplied using a supported exposure methodology, not inferred from illustrative holdings or disclosure language.","An operative SFC designation requires evidence of an actual designation; risk factors or the possibility of designation are insufficient.","Unknown scope, exposure or designation facts remain unknown. Absence of designation evidence is not evidence of no designation."],"citations":[{"quote":"funds that are authorised by the SFC for offering to the public in Hong Kong (Funds)6","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u4.564"},{"quote":"6 Except for listed closed-ended alternative asset funds (LAFs).","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691"},{"quote":"A Fund will be considered as a complex product if its total direct and indirect exposures to private market assets amount to 50% or more of the Fund’s NAV.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779"},{"quote":"On a case-by-case basis, the SFC may also designate a Fund as a complex product, taking into account factors including, without limitation:","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779"},{"quote":"the SFC will adopt a holistic approach taking into account the specific circumstances of the case.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u29.4630"},{"quote":"In cases where the Fund’s aggregate direct and indirect exposures to private market assets are less than 50% of the Fund’s NAV.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"},{"quote":"including but not limited to ensuring the suitability of the Fund for its investors irrespective of whether solicitation or recommendation is involved.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u32.4805"},{"quote":"Fund managers are encouraged to consult the SFC at the earliest opportunity if they are in doubt regarding complex product classification of their Funds.","unit_id":"d4148dd852cee.u49.6955"}],"distinction":"The substantive distinction is automatic classification at the inclusive 50% threshold versus an actual discretionary SFC designation below it. Neither private-market exposure alone nor an adverse risk factor automatically establishes classification. LAF exclusion removes this circular's route without establishing that a LAF is non-complex under other rules. The text supports this single classification reading more strongly than competing automatic-classification rules; uncertainty chiefly concerns measurement, timing and missing evidence.","family":"modality","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"Whether the assessed fund is authorised by the SFC for offering to the public in Hong Kong at the assessment time.","name":"public_sfc_authorised","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u4.564"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether the assessed fund is a listed closed-ended alternative asset fund within the footnote 6 exclusion.","name":"is_laf","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u63.8691"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether the Fund's total direct and indirect exposure to private market assets amounts to at least 50% of its NAV at the assessment time, using the applicable methodology. Missing or unresolved measurement evidence leaves this fact unknown.","name":"aggregate_exposure_at_least_half_nav","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u1.5","d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u59.7979"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether an SFC case-by-case designation of this Fund as a complex product under this circular is operative at the assessment time. Mere designation risk or missing records does not establish either truth value.","name":"operative_sfc_designation","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(or aggregate_exposure_at_least_half_nav operative_sfc_designation)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and public_sfc_authorised (not is_laf))"},"local_id":"classification_routes","questions":["How is aggregate exposure measured and evidenced for the Fund at the relevant time?","Is there an actual operative SFC designation, rather than only circumstances that could justify one?","If exposure subsequently falls below 50%, what rules govern continued classification?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Selected control: whether the retained circular's complex-product classification trigger is satisfied for an in-scope Fund at the assessment time. True means aggregate direct and indirect private-market exposure reaches at least 50% of NAV, or an operative SFC case-by-case designation exists, so the Fund must be treated as complex for distribution under this reading. False means both routes are affirmatively absent; it does not establish general non-complex status, compliance with sales duties or exemption under other instruments. An out-of-scope Fund receives no classification decision from this control. Missing evidence remains unresolved rather than producing false.","subject":"Complex-product classification trigger for an SFC-authorised public Fund, excluding LAFs"}]}},"java_checks":[],"live_provider":true,"model_calls":3,"no_progress":0,"nodes":[],"pending":null,"provider_id":"codex.fresh.v1.compact.v2","retrievals":[],"rounds":0,"roundtrips":[],"run_id":"run.08f45e4d9030408999f87203f067aefc","stop":null}